cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CyberLite, please cite this repository and the eventual paper."
title: "CyberLite: Resource-Efficient Post-Training of Sub-Billion-Parameter Language Models for Cybersecurity and Context-Aware Autocompletion"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "CyberLite Contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/braydos-h/CyberLite"
url: "https://github.com/braydos-h/CyberLite"
abstract: >-
  CyberLite is an open research project investigating whether a sub-billion-parameter
  language model can be post-trained into a practical, locally deployable cybersecurity
  assistant using LoRA/QLoRA, knowledge distillation, retrieval augmentation, and
  quantization. The repository provides a reproducible data pipeline, training and
  inference tooling, evaluation harnesses, and a paper scaffold. No trained research checkpoint or verified benchmark result is
  released in version 0.1.0.
keywords:
  - cybersecurity
  - large language models
  - parameter-efficient fine-tuning
  - LoRA
  - QLoRA
  - knowledge distillation
  - quantization
  - reproducibility
  - low-resource computing
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-25"
references:
  - type: generic
    title: "CyberLite paper (work in progress; results are placeholders)"
    notes: "A publication-ready manuscript scaffold is included under paper/. It contains no verified benchmark results yet."
